        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "a1010714-c3b8-5410-b11d-4a34b5fa8dcc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: R Adams Cowley, Dwight D. Eisenhower\n- Organizations: R Adams Cowley Shock Trauma Center\n- Roles: surgeon, President of the United States, Army general\n- Concepts: trauma medicine, emergency medicine, shock trauma, open-heart surgery, pacemaker\n\nFacts:\n- Dwight D. Eisenhower was an American politician and Army general who served as the 34th President of the United States from 1953 to 1961.\n- R Adams Cowley was born on July 25, 1917, and died on October 27, 1991.\n- R Adams Cowley was an American surgeon known as the \"Father of Trauma Medicine\" and was considered a pioneer in emergency medicine and the treatment of shock trauma.\n- R Adams Cowley was among the first surgeons to perform open-heart surgery.\n- R Adams Cowley invented a surgical clamp that bears his name.\n- R Adams Cowley created a prototype pacemaker that was used by Dwight D. Eisenhower.\n- Shock Trauma was founded by R Adams Cowley.\n- R Adams Cowley is considered the father of trauma medicine.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "6db9d4de-96fe-57e9-9de1-9d1452c39418",
        "text": "Page: R Adams Cowley. Sentence: R Adams Cowley (July 25, 1917 – October 27, 1991), the \"Father of Trauma Medicine,\" was an American surgeon considered a pioneer in emergency medicine and the treatment of shock trauma.\nPage: R Adams Cowley. Sentence: He is also known for being one of the first surgeons to perform open-heart surgery and invented both a surgical clamp that bears his name and a prototype pacemaker that was used by Dwight D. Eisenhower.\nPage: Dwight D. Eisenhower. Sentence: Dwight David \"Ike\" Eisenhower ( ; October 14, 1890 – March 28, 1969) was an American politician and Army general who served as the 34th President of the United States from 1953 until 1961.\nPage: R Adams Cowley Shock Trauma Center. Sentence: Shock Trauma was founded by R Adams Cowley, who is considered the father of trauma medicine.",
